From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Report the CPUs a PS5 game may run on.

Wine took the number of processors from sysconf, 16 on the console. A
game process runs on CPUs 0-12 only (its affinity is 0x1fff), and threads
of one priority there never share a CPU: measured with a probe, 13 busy
threads all start at once, a 14th waits until one of them stops, and 20
leave 7 waiting. A program that starts a worker per reported CPU, as
modern engines and DXVK's compiler pool do, therefore had three that did
not run until another blocked. Report the CPUs the process may run on,
from cpuset_getaffinity, and keep sysconf's count if the call fails.

  dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
  1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
index a4e8292..a8b5939 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
@@ -1764,6 +1764,28 @@ static void get_random( void *buf, ULONG len )
  *
  * Init a couple of places with CPU related information.
  */
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+/* sys/cpuset.h's cpuset_t is wider than the set the console's kernel takes,
+ * which is 64 bits wide (measured), so declare the call with that. */
+extern int cpuset_getaffinity( int level, int which, id_t id, size_t size, ULONGLONG *mask );
+
+/* A game runs on CPUs 0-12 of the console's 16 (measured: its affinity is
+ * 0x1fff), and threads of one priority there never share a CPU, so a program
+ * that starts a worker per reported CPU would have three that do not run
+ * until another blocks. Report the CPUs the process may run on instead of
+ * the ones online. */
+static long ps5_process_cpus( long online )
+{
+    ULONGLONG mask = 0;
+
+    if (cpuset_getaffinity( 3 /* CPU_LEVEL_WHICH */, 2 /* CPU_WHICH_PID */, -1, sizeof(mask), &mask ) || !mask)
+        return online;
+    /* Windows numbers CPUs from 0 and so does the console: a set that is not
+     * 0..n-1 keeps the highest one, so every CPU the process has is named. */
+    return 64 - __builtin_clzll( mask );
+}
+#endif
+
 void init_cpu_info(void)
 {
     long num;
@@ -1775,6 +1797,9 @@ void init_cpu_info(void)
         num = 1;
         WARN("Failed to detect the number of processors.\n");
     }
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    num = ps5_process_cpus( num );
+#endif
 #elif defined(CTL_HW) && defined(HW_NCPU)
     int mib[2];
     size_t len = sizeof(num);
